{{Term/Store|Royal Guard Uniform|Royal Guard Uniforms|Series, BotW, TotK, AoC|plural}} are recurring [[Item]]s in {{TLoZ Series}}.{{Exp Game|BotW, TotK, AoC}}<ref name="BotW Inventory"/><ref name="TotK Inventory"/><ref name="AoC Allies"/>

==Location and Uses==
==={{BotW|-}}===
{{Descriptions BotW}}
The Royal Guard Uniform appears exclusively in {{TCB}} [[Downloadable Content]] pack. It is a part of the [[Royal Guard Set]], along with the [[Royal Guard Cap]] and [[Royal Guard Boots]].<ref name="CaC 190"/> Wearing the full [[Armor Set]] will decrease the amount of [[Stamina]] required for a charge attack. The Uniform available through the "[[EX Royal Guard Rumors]]" [[Side Quest]], which requires [[Link]] to read the ''[[Super Rumor Mill V4]]'' at [[Riverside Stable]].<ref name="BotW Adventure Log"/> The [[Book]] claims that pieces of the Royal Guard Set can be found in the [[Dining Hall]], near the [[Guards' Chamber]], and on the second floor.<ref name="BotW Super Rumor Mill V4"/>

The Royal Guard Uniform can be found in a [[Hidden Chest]] behind a bombable wall in the [[Hyrule Castle Corridors]]. This wall is located near the Dining Hall. After collecting it, [[Granté]] will begin to sell the Royal Guard Uniform in [[Tarrey Town]].{{Note|Prior to the [[The Legend of Zelda: Breath of the Wild#Updates|Version 1.3.3 Update]], Granté would not sell any Armor that is exclusive to the ''[[Breath of the Wild Expansion Pass]]''. This meant that the Royal Guard Uniform could not be replaced if sold.}} The Royal Guard Uniform cannot be enhanced by a [[Great Fairy]], nor can it be [[Dye]]d at the [[Kochi Dye Shop]].

==={{TotK|-}}===
{{Descriptions TotK}}
{{Stub|TotK}}
The Royal Guard Uniform is found in a [[Treasure Chest]] in the [[Guards' Chamber]].

